# modbusspec-sweep 0: requests to a real device in the order sent, and their replies
device: inverter/goodwe/et
product: GoodWe ESA series, GW15K-ETA-G20 (firmware 04098-01-S51 and 02203-03-S01 at 35021), 2 battery modules
unit: 247
link: Modbus TCP, port 502, from a tablet on the site's LAN
date: 2026-11-12, 15:25:26 to 15:34:37 (+01:00); function 04 got no reply, and the sweep stopped in its first pass
tool: SolarDash 0.6.3 (85) register sweep, read only (functions 43/14, 03, 04); its passes are the comment lines below
masked: 'digits of serial numbers (inverter at 2000, 35003, 45203; battery at 22000, 22021, 37060) as #; their letters are kept'
format: 'function address+count[*runs] reply. A run of n requests: each starting where the one before ended, same count, same reply. Reply: E code for an
  exception, S for no reply (a request sent again after it is a line of its own), or the words in hex, w*n for n equal words, M and two characters for
  a masked word (# a hidden digit). 43/14 lines: Read Device Identification, code object reply.'
